From 11c9dc5fe63e473f79f6f4d70528a50102a5eece Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CaptainPhantasy <DouglasTalley1977@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Apr 2026 06:33:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] feat: transcript-text behavioral classifier with
 enforcement chain

Adds behavior-classifier.ts with three detectors:
- detectUnwantedQuestions: model asks clarifying/permission questions
- detectUnsubstantiatedCompletion: model claims done without evidence
- detectIgnoredDirective: model violates explicit user directives

Wired into observer pipeline:
- runBehavioralAnalysis() called on session_shutdown
- classifyBehavior() runs on all session observations
- Detected violations auto-create active instincts (confidence >= 0.7)
- Instinct IDs use kebab-case (Zod schema compliant)

10 regression tests proving:
- Each violation type is detected from model text output
- Substantiated completions are NOT false-positived
- Directive extraction finds MUST/NEVER/ALWAYS markers
- Violations persist as instincts across storage instances
- Full chain: violation text -> instinct -> enforcement block text

Chain: model output text -> classifyBehavior() -> writeInstinct() ->
reloadActiveInstincts() -> context handler -> <learned-rules> in model context
